  "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B043",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B019",
    "B008"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration has changed from B019 to B043. The three-jet discovery remains a fundamental experimental landmark, but this final discussion has made its unresolved three-person attribution too consequential to set aside. B043 instead joins a sharply defined physical idea with decisive realization, exceptional demonstrated maturity, and a compact credit line. The magic-wavelength lattice-clock achievement created a durable new regime of atomic control and precision measurement, with Katori and Ye representing invention and defining experimental development in a way that can be stated plainly and audited rigorously.",
    "case_against": "B043 is an enabling measurement technology rather than the direct observation of a new constituent of matter, and its citation must not annex the wider later ecosystem of clock architectures, frequency-comb work, comparisons, or metrological refinements. The historical record must still confirm that the boundary of the original invention and realization supports precisely the Katori-Ye allocation.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce judges B043 preferable to B019 because optical lattice clocks have a sharper and more defensible credit line, whereas the gluon observation was collaboration-scale.",
        "response": "I now agree with the force of this distinction. It is not a vote against the scientific magnitude of B019; rather, a Nobel citation must identify both an achievement and the people behind it. Until the historical audit can show why Wolf, Söding, and Wu are the uniquely defensible representation of the three-jet observation, B043 is the more complete public configuration."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll emphasizes the unified lattice-clock narrative: Katori's magic-wavelength concept, Ye's decisive realization, independent reproduction, and sustained precision-measurement impact.",
        "response": "This supplies the decisive reason for my revision. The achievement is not merely an incremental improvement in timekeeping: it made a many-atom interrogation regime possible without the usual trapping shift. Its demonstrated reproducibility and clear conceptual-experimental sequence meet the maturity and attribution tests simultaneously, provided we keep the citation tightly bounded."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that B021 revealed the observable physical significance of quantum phase, while acknowledging that the Aharonov-Bohm and Berry effects have distinct histories.",
        "response": "I retain strong admiration for B021's conceptual reach and experimental confirmation. But the stated qualification remains material at the final stage: one citation would have to join two separate discoveries without obscuring either. B043 has a more singular achievement and a less strained account of individual credit."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical documentation delimits the original magic-wavelength lattice-clock invention and decisive realization from later metrological advances while fully confirming the Katori-Ye attribution.",
      "Whether a priority audit could yet establish Wolf, Söding, and Wu as the uniquely most defensible three-person representation of the B019 discovery.",
      "Whether B021 can be formulated as one prize-defining achievement without conflating the distinct histories of the Aharonov-Bohm and Berry effects."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile; no new conflict has emerged."
  }
}
